CREATED:20260501T204445Z
DESCRIPTION:ADF Co-Commission\nProgram: bLUr\nRunning time: 60 minutes\, n
 o intermission\nTickets: $30-$45\nTickets are purchased through Duke Univ
 ersity's Box Office.\n\nPost-Performance Discussion\n\nCompany Website: w
 ww.daela.org\n\nCulled from the haunting experience of having witnessed a
  loved one overdose\, bLUr exists within a landscape of physical and emot
 ional crisis. Built in cycles of deeply erotic tenderness and fierce comp
 assion\, five performers of exquisite humanity fly through states of chao
 s\, panic\, emptiness\, clarity\, hope\, and back\, arresting their cycle
 s intermittently to perform urgent interventions\, tender and brutal resc
 ues. Like a body seized by howling hunger\, their wild encounters are urg
 ent and essential\, providing the glue that keeps this fragile space inta
 ct. In bLUr\, time warps and haunts\, reminding us of our fragility\, pow
 er\, and need to care for and rescue one another.\n\nPhoto Credit: Maria 
 Baranova\n_________\n\nADF offers a 20% discount to Duke employees and $2
 0 tickets to Duke students (restrictions apply). To access your discount\
 , just log in with your Duke Net ID at tickets.duke.edu.
DURATION:PT1H
DTSTAMP:20260501T204625Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260627T193000
LAST-MODIFIED:20260501T204625Z
