CREATED:20260611T134139Z
DESCRIPTION:For centuries\, the church has marked the transition from dayt
 ime to evening with psalms\, prayer\, and song. This Choral Evensong serv
 ice follows this historic pattern\, using the liturgy of the Book of Comm
 on Prayer and featuring choral and organ music from the English cathedral
  tradition. The service is led by participants in the Royal School of Chu
 rch Music in America Carolina Summer Choral Residency. Through this weekl
 ong course\, leading church musicians train girl choristers and adult sin
 gers in sacred music.\n\nParking is available on a first-come-first-serve
 d basis in the Bryan Center garage at 125 Science Drive. ADA parking is a
 vailable in the Bryan Center Surface Lot at the same address.\n\nThe serv
 ice is livestreamed on the Duke Chapel YouTube channel and broadcast live
  on channel 12 of the Duke Hospital TV system and channel 110 of the Duke
  Campus Vision TV system.
DURATION:PT1H
